{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01XLtEKHHqnu7r5hW3ScsRWz", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/common/001552331.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/common/001537447.docx\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/en/H30-00804.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://tabi-mag.jp/ky0340/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/H30-00804.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://yamap.com/activities/47046904/article\"}, {\"url\": \"https://tabi-mag.jp/tag/%e5%be%8c%e9%86%8d%e9%86%90%e5%a4%a9%e7%9a%87/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://tabi-mag.jp/tag/%e7%a3%a8%e5%b4%96%e4%bb%8f/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://kansai-u.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/4994/files/KU-1100-20170301-13.pdf\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:35:37.771Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "相者 四十歳まで 東大寺 笠置 修行 僧", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_017yqSD9qxiZKZX3LR8zjADX", "content": [{"title": "www.mlit.go.jp", "url": "https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/common/001552331.pdf"}, {"title": "www.mlit.go.jp", "url": "https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/common/001537447.docx"}, {"title": "Title Kasagidera Temple", "url": "https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/en/H30-00804.html"}, {"title": "tabi-mag.jp", "url": "https://tabi-mag.jp/ky0340/"}, {"title": "タイトル 笠置寺 概要", "url": "https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/H30-00804.html"}, {"title": "yamap.com", "url": "https://yamap.com/activities/47046904/article"}, {"title": "tabi-mag.jp", "url": "https://tabi-mag.jp/tag/%e5%be%8c%e9%86%8d%e9%86%90%e5%a4%a9%e7%9a%87/"}, {"title": "tabi-mag.jp", "url": "https://tabi-mag.jp/tag/%e7%a3%a8%e5%b4%96%e4%bb%8f/"}, {"title": "KU 1100 20170301 13", "url": "https://kansai-u.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/4994/files/KU-1100-20170301-13.pdf"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything about a 相者 who trained at Tōdaiji or Kasagi until age 40, so I can't confirm that claim. The results do cover Kasagi-dera's ties to Tōdaiji and its role as a monastic training site:\n\n- **Founding figures:** Kasagi-dera's origins are traced to Ryōben and his disciple Jitchū, both linked to Tōdaiji, who carved Buddhist images into the rock surface. 笠置寺は、僧侶の厳しい修行の場として多くの信仰を集めました。 (Kasagi-dera gathered many believers as a site of rigorous monastic training.)\n- **Jitchū and Shōryōdō:** One source says the original Shōryōdō at Kasagi was built around 752 by Jitchū, and that it is considered the birthplace of Tōdaiji's \"Omizutori\" rite. 本来の正月堂は、752年頃に実忠によって建立。\n- **Jōkei:** A scholar-monk, Jōkei (1155–1213), lived at Kasagi in 1191, possibly to study, and was active in rebuilding the temple and founding a Miroku faith group. 学僧として名が高かった貞慶(1155－1213)が笠置寺に住していました。\n\nIf you can share the name of the monk or the source where you saw the \"相者\" and \"age 40\" detail, I can search for that specifically."], "durationSeconds": 5.8951646250000005, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01XLtEKHHqnu7r5hW3ScsRWz", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
