in", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genshin"}, {"title": "Ekai Kawaguchi", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ekai_Kawaguchi"}, {"title": "R%C5%8Dben", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C5%8Dben"}]}, "The search did not find a source that links a monk named Kasagi to physiognomy and a Tōdaiji retreat. The closest hits are about the Tōdaiji Shuni'e rite and a different Mount Kasagi story.\n\n- **Shuni'e retreat:** A PDF on the Tōdaiji Shuni'e describes a yearly ritual retreat in which a group of about forty people enter the retreat and live together for a month. The same source ties the rite's origins to Mount Kasagi, where a disciple of Rōben reportedly saw heavenly beings in 751. It does not mention physiognomy or a monk named Kasagi.\n- **Rōben:** Rōben was a clerical founder of Tōdaiji, and he died on November 16, 773, at the age of 85 near Uda, according to Wikipedia.\n- **Physiognomy:** The physiognomy results concern the Chinese text attributed to the monk Master Maiyi, not any Japanese monk named Kasagi.\n- **Mount Kasagi:** A separate Wikipedia entry covers Kasagi-dera, a fortified temple on Mount Kasagi where Emperor Go-Daigo had hidden the Japanese imperial regalia. It is unrelated to Tōdaiji or physiognomy.\n\nIf the \"Kasagi\" monk is a specific figure from a particular text, a search in Japanese (笠置 or 笠木 with 観相 and 東大寺) or a more specific name might find the source."], "durationSeconds": 6.03569775, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Uoz9M6wegVMM7r7A5jLXaw", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
